  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1223 PM CST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nAs of noon, stratus persists for areas east of a line from\nNorfolk to Lincoln. For the rest of the day, this will be pretty\n\"steady state\", but is expected to expand this evening into\ntonight. \n\nThe increasing cloud cover will keep most areas (except for \nnortheastern Nebraska) above freezing tonight. Late tonight into\nFriday morning, some patchy drizzle will become possible as the\ndepth of low-level saturation increases and coincides with some\nweak lift. Impacts should be minimal and the most favored area\nfor this is near and south of Interstate-80. \n\nLingering cloud cover will help keep temperatures a bit on the\ncooler side again Friday (upper 40s and low 50s). Friday night\nwill feature another opportunity for subfreezing temperatures as\nsurface high pressure pushes to our east. After that,\ntemperatures look very mild through the weekend and into next\nweek (highs in the 60s and low temperatures in thu upper 30s and\n40s).\n\nDry conditions are also favored to accompany this relatively\nwarm pattern. Global ensembles highlight a high-confidence\nstretch of dry conditions for Friday through at least next\nWednesday. Even beyond that, precipitation potential appears\npretty limited through the middle of November.",
